  "slug": "visual-autoencoders-0ca5",
  "summary": "Dynamical and decoding descriptors now span human MEG, rodent EEG and mouse fMRI, moving beyond static pairwise correlation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is quantitative characterization of brain dynamics across scales and modalities, beyond static pairwise correlation. Resting-state human MEG coarse-graining reports power-law scaling and avalanche invariance, with exponents tied to a criticality framework. A whole-cortex mouse network with directed Allen-atlas connectivity reproduces fMRI co-activation patterns through attractor dynamics. A separate rat EEG study applies an asynchronous recurrent decoder to predict self-paced locomotion speed (r=0.88) from 32 skull electrodes, addressing behavioral readout rather than model structure. These items do not test a shared model. What is new is the pairing of scale-dependent, dynamical and decoding descriptors across human MEG, rodent EEG and mouse fMRI.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-02-25"
}
